            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Soup Loving Nicole"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The cocktail sauce poured over the top is a must. I still feel it lacked. You really need more than just the Worcestershire i the ball itself. Old Bay is the first thing that comes to mind. Add a teaspoon of that and I think it would be perfect. Imitation crab is really sweet so it needs something to offset that.",
            "datePublished": "2024-04-30T02:51:39.270Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yes I rolled it in ground almonds also I added a little garlic. I put the cocktail sauce on the side. It is great.",
            "datePublished": "2025-12-17T09:45:14.978Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "fruitdog"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Nice recipe, but needed more for us. Hot sauce and Old Bay to the mix and horseradish to the cocktail sauce that tops this dish. Definitely use the cocktail!",
            "datePublished": "2021-12-27T05:52:01.273Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karen Ford"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have made this recipe for at least 30 years. I add garlic that is finely chopped, also finely chopped green or red pepper adds color, and I add 1/4 cup mayonaisse to make it in to a dip. I always taste for salt and black or white pepper as I do not use as much Worchestershire sauce.\nI realized it would be a hit when I took it to a Super Bowl party and the guys ate the entire double batch by half-time.",
            "datePublished": "2011-12-31T11:06:20.207Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Debbie H"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This cheese ball is great. I used 1 can of crabmeat instead of the imitation crab. I meant to add a little Tony Chachere's Creole seasoning but forgot. So we sprinkled it on as we ate it and it definitely helped bring out the crab flavor. So next time I will add it to the recipe. Will definitely make again.",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-02T19:53:01.947Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "pj"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent!!!!!!!!! I used scallions and a bit of fresh basil and cilantro (have a herb garden) The second time had real crab and shrimp on hand very amazing! Love this recipe any way you choose. I ate the entire thing myself and had to make another the next day for it's intended purpose (a party)!",
            "datePublished": "2009-09-08T07:27:53.890Z"
          },
          {
